            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1042-3680(17)30110-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.nec.2017.09.014</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Degenerative cervical myelopathy (DCM) is the most common cause of nontraumatic spinal cord injury worldwide. Even relatively mild impairment in functional scores can significantly impact daily activities. Surgery is an effective treatment for DCM, but outcomes are dependent on more than technique and preoperative neurologic deficits.</AbstractText>
